  sumEn="For four hundred years the men who ruled Wales from London treated Welsh as something to be got rid of. An Act of Parliament shut it out of the courts, a government report called it a ‘vast drawback’, and schools hung a block of wood round the necks of children who spoke it. Wales refused to let it go.",
